<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech c.bank lists largest domestic, foreign banks.</title>
<headline>Czech c.bank lists largest domestic, foreign banks.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is a list of the Czech Republic's 10 domestic and foreign banks, ranked by basic capital, as of February 28, 1997:</p>
<p>    Domestic banks		   Basic capital</p>
<p>					    (in bln CZK)</p>
<p> 1. Komercni Banka a.s.	9.50</p>
<p> 2. Ceska Sporitelna a.s.    7.60</p>
<p> 3. IPB a.s.		     5.68</p>
<p> 4. CSOB a.s.				  5.11</p>
<p> 5. Agrobanka a.s.			   3.49</p>
<p> 6. Banka Hana a.s.	    2.70</p>
<p> 7. Pragobanka a.s.			  1.86</p>
<p> 8. Universal Banka a.s.		   1.60</p>
<p>9. Zivnostenska Banka a.s.  1.36 10. Union Banka a.s. 1.34</p>
<p>    Foreign banks		    Basic capital</p>
<p>					    (in bln CZK)</p>
<p> 1. Vereinsbank (CZ) a.s.		  1.50</p>
<p> 2. Interbanka a.s.			  1.25</p>
<p> 3. Creditanstalt a.s.		     1.247</p>
<p> 4. BNP-Dresdner (CR) a.s.		 1.00</p>
<p> 5. Societe Generale Banka a.s.	  0.774</p>
<p> 6. Hypo-Bank CZ a.s.			0.740</p>
<p> 7. Citibank a.s.			    0.600</p>
<p>Note. Figures supplied by the Czech National Bank (CNB). Agrobanka is currently under central bank temporary administration due to liquidity problems following the collapse of Kreditni Banka a.s..</p>
<p>The CNB has set out plans to split Agrobanka's assets into two parts -- questionable and sound -- allowing for the sound assets to be sold off in a tender while the questionable assets will be retained and &quot;their value realised&quot;.</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 420-2-2423-0003</p>
</text>
